class:: TNegBinomialRand
summary:: Triggered negative-binomial failures sampler
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Distributions
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/TGammaRand, Classes/TPoissonRand

description::

The Negative Binomial distribution generalizes the Geometric distribution, modeling the number of failures before achieving a specific N number of successes. Mathematically, this provides an integer-based distribution that can be tuned to cluster and disperse values more flexibly than the geometric model. Conceptually, it is excellent for complex generative timekeeping, algorithmic burst counting, or scheduling complex, integer-based rhythmic delays.

Returns failures before code::successes:: successes. It draws a gamma intensity and then a Poisson count, so positive real success counts are supported.

Like link::Classes/TPoissonRand::, it returns nonnegative counts; unlike Poisson, the gamma–Poisson mixture permits overdispersion controlled by success probability and count.

subsection:: Probability mass

image::negative-binomial-mass.png#Failures before two successes for probability = 0.25, 0.5, and 0.75, shown in muted teal, blue, and plum. Lower success probability shifts mass toward larger counts and increases dispersion.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: successes
Strictly positive real success count.
argument:: probability
Success probability. At or above one returns zero; at or below zero returns the largest exact integer float.
argument:: trig
Resample on a rising edge.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Restore the seed and sample a new initial value.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ TNegBinomialRand.kr(3, 0.4, Impulse.kr(5)).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar((TNegBinomialRand.kr(2, 0.6, Impulse.kr(8)) + 1) * 100, 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

code::
// Algorithmic Burst Counting
(
{
    var trig, bursts, sig;
    trig = Impulse.kr(4);
    // Generalizes geometric waits, providing clustered, integer-based rhythmic scatter
    bursts = TNegBinomialRand.kr(successes: 3, probability: 0.5, trig: trig);
    sig = Blip.ar((bursts * 50) + 100, bursts + 1) * EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.01, 0.2), trig);
    Pan2.ar(sig * 0.1)
}.play;
)
::
